-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1: THE SCHEDULE (modification of the Act for certain contracts) and the subsections that point at it
-- (ss 11(5), 12(6), 13(4), 14(6), 15(3), 35(8)).
-- Every function here takes `the date the contract was made`.  A window the Schedule states in its own words
-- ("made before 18 May 1973", "on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May 1985") is a limit in the text's own
-- wording, so a contract outside the window gets NOTHING from that paragraph (the unmodified section answers it),
-- and a contract inside it gets the paragraph's answer.  Paragraphs 7 and 8 are deleted; ss 15(3) and 35(8) still
-- refer to them.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`
IMPORT `soga-part2-formation`
IMPORT `soga-part7-supplementary`
IMPORT `soga-interpretation`

DECLARE `Matter to which regard shall be had in judging whether reliance on a term is fair or reasonable` IS ONE OF
    `the strength of the bargaining positions of the seller and buyer relative to each other, taking into account, among other things, the availability of suitable alternative products and sources of supply`
    `whether the buyer received an inducement to agree to the term or in accepting it had an opportunity of buying the goods or suitable alternatives without it from any source of supply`
    `whether the buyer knew or ought reasonably to have known of the existence and extent of the term, having regard, among other things, to any custom of the trade and any previous course of dealing between the parties`
    `where the term exempts from all or any of the provisions of section 13, 14 or 15 if some condition is not complied with, whether it was reasonable at the time of the contract to expect that compliance with that condition would be practicable`
    `whether the goods were manufactured, processed, or adapted to the special order of the buyer`
    `any other circumstance of the case`

-- A window test used by every paragraph of the Schedule.
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the window` IS A DATE
      `the first day after the window` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `helper (Schedule): the date falls within the window` IS
    (`the date asked about` AT LEAST `the first day of the window`) AND (NOT (`the date asked about` AT LEAST `the first day after the window`))

§ `The Schedule -- modification of the Act for certain contracts`

§§ `The subsections that point at the Schedule`

-- s 11(5).
-- src:363 | (5) Paragraph 2 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:364 | made before 22 April 1967.
@ref s 11(5) (src:363-364)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(5) paragraph 2 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 22 4 1967))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 2 applies "in relation to a contract made before 22 April 1967". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 12(6).
-- src:416 | (6) Paragraph 3 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:417 | made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 12(6) (src:416-417)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(6) paragraph 3 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 3 applies "in relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 13(4).
-- src:436 | (4) Paragraph 4 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:437 | made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 13(4) (src:436-437)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13(4) paragraph 4 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 4 applies "in relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 14(6), paragraph 5.
-- src:513 | (6) Paragraph 5 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:514 | made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May 1985, and
-- src:515 | paragraph 6 in relation to one made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 14(6) para 5 (src:513-515)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(6) paragraph 5 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `helper (Schedule): the date falls within the window` `the date the contract was made` (Date 18 5 1973) (Date 19 5 1985)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 5 applies "in relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May 1985". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 14(6), paragraph 6.
-- src:513 | (6) Paragraph 5 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract
-- src:514 | made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May 1985, and
-- src:515 | paragraph 6 in relation to one made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 14(6) para 6 (src:513-515)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(6) paragraph 6 of the Schedule applies in relation to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 6 applies "in relation to one made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

