    BRANCH
        IF `the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 3 applies "In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention, there is ... (b) an implied warranty"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless" is read as the text's no when the circumstances show a different intention.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1675 | 3. In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973, substitute the following for
-- src:1676 | section 12:
-- src:1678 | . “Implied terms about title, etc.
-- src:1680 | 12. In a contract of sale, unless the circumstances of the contract are
