-- src:1688 | (b) an implied warranty that the buyer will have and enjoy
-- src:1689 | quiet possession of the goods;
@ref sch para 3 s 12(b) breach (src:1675-1681) (src:1688-1689)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer has and enjoys quiet possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 3 s 12(b) the implied warranty of quiet possession is broken` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the warranty is implied in a contract "made before 18 May 1973" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention" -- the exception takes the case out and the text says nothing further.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `the buyer has and enjoys quiet possession of the goods`)

-- paragraph 3, limb (c): the implied warranty that the goods will be free from any charge or encumbrance.
