-- src:1675 | 3. In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973, substitute the following for
-- src:1676 | section 12:
-- src:1678 | . “Implied terms about title, etc.
-- src:1680 | 12. In a contract of sale, unless the circumstances of the contract are
-- src:1681 | such as to show a different intention, there is —
-- src:1691 | (c) an implied warranty that the goods will be free from any
-- src:1692 | charge or encumbrance in favour of any third party, not
-- src:1693 | declared or known to the buyer before or at the time when
-- src:1694 | the contract is made.”.
@ref sch para 3 s 12(c) breach (src:1675-1681) (src:1691-1694)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are subject to a charge or encumbrance in favour of a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was declared or known to the buyer before or at the time when the contract is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 3 s 12(c) the implied warranty of freedom from charge or encumbrance is broken` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the warranty is implied in a contract "made before 18 May 1973" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the circumstances of the contract are such as to show a different intention" -- the exception takes the case out and the text says nothing further.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the goods are subject to a charge or encumbrance in favour of a third party` AND (NOT `it was declared or known to the buyer before or at the time when the contract is made`))

