§§ `Paragraph 5 -- section 14 as it stood for a contract made from 18 May 1973 to 18 May 1985`

-- paragraph 5, s 14(1).
-- src:1706 | 5. In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May
-- src:1707 | 1985, substitute the following for section 14:
-- src:1711 | 14.—(1) Except as provided by this section and section 15 and
-- src:1712 | subject to any other enactment, there is no implied condition or
-- src:1713 | warranty about the quality or fitness for any particular purpose of
-- src:1714 | goods supplied under a contract of sale.
@ref sch para 5 s 14(1) (src:1706-1707) (src:1711-1714)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `section 14 as substituted or section 15 provides an implied condition or warranty on these facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another enactment provides an implied condition or warranty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 5 s 14(1) there is an implied condition or warranty about the quality or fitness of the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`helper (Schedule): the date falls within the window` `the date the contract was made` (Date 18 5 1973) (Date 19 5 1985))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 5 applies "In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May 1985". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `another enactment provides an implied condition or warranty`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any other enactment", which is not among the sources.
            NOTHING
        IF `section 14 as substituted or section 15 provides an implied condition or warranty on these facts`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as provided by this section and section 15" -- the provision that provides it gives the answer.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is no implied condition or warranty about the quality or fitness for any particular purpose of goods supplied under a contract of sale"
            JUST FALSE

-- paragraph 5, s 14(2): merchantable quality.
-- src:1706 | 5. In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May
-- src:1707 | 1985, substitute the following for section 14:
-- src:1716 | (2) Where the seller sells goods in the course of a business, there is an
-- src:1717 | implied condition that the goods supplied under the contract are of
-- src:1718 | merchantable quality, except that there is no such condition —
-- src:1720 | (a) as regards defects specifically drawn to the buyer’s
-- src:1721 | attention before the contract is made; or
-- src:1723 | (b) if the buyer examines the goods before the contract is
-- src:1724 | made, as regards defects which that examination ought to
-- src:1725 | reveal.
@ref sch para 5 s 14(2) (src:1706-1707) (src:1716-1725)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `the seller sells the goods in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 5 s 14(2) there is an implied condition that the goods supplied are of merchantable quality` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`helper (Schedule): the date falls within the window` `the date the contract was made` (Date 18 5 1973) (Date 19 5 1985))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 5 applies "In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May 1985". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the seller sells the goods in the course of a business`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition is implied "Where the seller sells goods in the course of a business". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1706 | 5. In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May
-- src:1707 | 1985, substitute the following for section 14:
-- src:1716 | (2) Where the seller sells goods in the course of a business, there is an
-- src:1717 | implied condition that the goods supplied under the contract are of
-- src:1718 | merchantable quality, except that there is no such condition —
-- src:1720 | (a) as regards defects specifically drawn to the buyer’s
-- src:1721 | attention before the contract is made; or
-- src:1723 | (b) if the buyer examines the goods before the contract is
-- src:1724 | made, as regards defects which that examination ought to
-- src:1725 | reveal.
@ref sch para 5 s 14(2) breach (src:1706-1707) (src:1716-1725)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `the seller sells the goods in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are of merchantable quality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defects were specifically drawn to the buyer's attention before the contract was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer examined the goods before the contract was made and the defects are ones which that examination ought to reveal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 5 s 14(2) the implied condition of merchantable quality is broken` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`helper (Schedule): the date falls within the window` `the date the contract was made` (Date 18 5 1973) (Date 19 5 1985))) OR (NOT `the seller sells the goods in the course of a business`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition is implied only under paragraph 5's window and "Where the seller sells goods in the course of a business". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (ab): a period the text fixes in its own words, and a "where" condition: outside the period, or with the condition not met, the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the defects were specifically drawn to the buyer's attention before the contract was made` OR `the buyer examined the goods before the contract was made and the defects are ones which that examination ought to reveal`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that there is no such condition (a) as regards defects specifically drawn to the buyer’s attention before the contract is made; or (b) if the buyer examines the goods before the contract is made, as regards defects which that examination ought to reveal"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "except that there is no such condition" is read as the text's no, so there is no breach as regards those defects.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `the goods are of merchantable quality`)

