      `this or another Act provides an implied condition or warranty on these facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 6 s 14(1) there is an implied condition or warranty about the quality or fitness of the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 6 applies "In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `this or another Act provides an implied condition or warranty on these facts`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this and any other Act" -- the provision that provides it gives the answer.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is no implied condition or warranty about the quality or fitness for any particular purpose of goods supplied under a contract of sale"
            JUST FALSE

-- paragraph 6, s 14(2): fitness for purpose.
-- src:1769 | 6. In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973, substitute the following for
-- src:1770 | section 14:
-- src:1778 | (2) Where the buyer, expressly or by implication, makes known to the
-- src:1779 | seller the particular purpose for which the goods are required, so as to
-- src:1780 | show that the buyer relies on the seller’s skill or judgment, and the
-- src:1781 | goods are of a description which it is in the course of the seller’s
-- src:1782 | business to supply (whether he is the manufacturer or not), there is an
-- src:1783 | implied condition that the goods will be reasonably fit for such
-- src:1784 | purpose, except that in the case of a contract for the sale of a specified
-- src:1785 | article under its patent or other trade name there is no implied condition
-- src:1786 | as to its fitness for any particular purpose.
