      `the goods are of a description which it is in the course of the seller's business to supply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of a specified article under its patent or other trade name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 6 s 14(2) there is an implied condition that the goods will be reasonably fit for such purpose` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 6 applies "In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`the buyer, expressly or by implication, makes known to the seller the particular purpose for which the goods are required, so as to show that the buyer relies on the seller's skill or judgment` AND `the goods are of a description which it is in the course of the seller's business to supply`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition is implied "Where the buyer ... makes known to the seller the particular purpose ... and the goods are of a description which it is in the course of the seller’s business to supply". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the contract is for the sale of a specified article under its patent or other trade name`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that in the case of a contract for the sale of a specified article under its patent or other trade name there is no implied condition as to its fitness for any particular purpose"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

