§§ `Paragraph 9 -- section 55 as it stood for a contract made from 18 May 1973 to 31 January 1978`

-- paragraph 9, s 55(1).
-- src:1810 | 9. In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February
-- src:1811 | 1978, substitute the following for section 55:
-- src:1815 | 55.—(1) Where a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract
-- src:1816 | of sale of goods by implication of law, it may be negatived or varied by
-- src:1817 | express agreement, or by the course of dealing between the parties, or
-- src:1818 | by such usage as binds both parties to the contract, but the preceding
-- src:1819 | provision has effect subject to the following provisions of this section.
@ref sch para 9 s 55(1) (src:1810-1811) (src:1815-1819)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale of goods by implication of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a following provision of section 55 as substituted prevents the negativing or variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the way` IS A `Way of negativing or varying a right, duty or liability implied by law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 9 s 55(1) the right, duty or liability may be negatived or varied` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`helper (Schedule): the date falls within the window` `the date the contract was made` (Date 18 5 1973) (Date 1 2 1978))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 9 applies "In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale of goods by implication of law`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale of goods by implication of law". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `a following provision of section 55 as substituted prevents the negativing or variation`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but the preceding provision has effect subject to the following provisions of this section"; the following provision decides.
            NOTHING
        IF `the way` EQUALS `express agreement` OR `the way` EQUALS `the course of dealing between the parties` OR `the way` EQUALS `such usage as binds both parties to the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names three ways and does not say that no other way will do.
            NOTHING

-- paragraph 9, s 55(2).
-- src:1810 | 9. In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February
-- src:1811 | 1978, substitute the following for section 55:
-- src:1821 | (2) An express condition or warranty does not negative a condition or
-- src:1822 | warranty implied by this Act unless inconsistent with it.
@ref sch para 9 s 55(2) (src:1810-1811) (src:1821-1822)
