§§ `Paragraph 10 -- section 55 as it stood for a contract made before 18 May 1973`

-- src:1933 | 10. In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973, substitute the following
-- src:1934 | for section 55:
-- src:1938 | 55. Where a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of
-- src:1939 | sale by implication of law, it may be negatived or varied by express
-- src:1940 | agreement, or by the course of dealing between the parties, or by such
-- src:1941 | usage as binds both parties to the contract.”.
@ref sch para 10 (src:1933-1934) (src:1938-1941)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale by implication of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the way` IS A `Way of negativing or varying a right, duty or liability implied by law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 10 s 55 the right, duty or liability may be negatived or varied` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 10 applies "In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale by implication of law`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where a right, duty or liability would arise under a contract of sale by implication of law". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the way` EQUALS `express agreement` OR `the way` EQUALS `the course of dealing between the parties` OR `the way` EQUALS `such usage as binds both parties to the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names three ways and does not say that no other way will do.
            NOTHING

