§§ `Paragraphs 12 and 13 -- the definition of business in section 61(1)`

-- paragraph 12.
-- src:1995 | 12. In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February
-- src:1996 | 1978, in the definition of “business” in section 61(1) for “or local or public
-- src:1997 | authority” substitute “, local authority or statutory undertaker”.
@ref sch para 12 (src:1995-1997)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `the activity is a trade or ordinary business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is a profession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is the activities of a Government department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is the activities of a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is the activities of a statutory undertaker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 12 the activity is a business` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`helper (Schedule): the date falls within the window` `the date the contract was made` (Date 18 5 1973) (Date 1 2 1978))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 12 applies "In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the activity is a trade or ordinary business` OR `the activity is a profession` OR `the activity is the activities of a Government department` OR `the activity is the activities of a local authority` OR `the activity is the activities of a statutory undertaker`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): “business” still “includes” the named activities; the list is not closed, and "public authority" is replaced by "local authority or statutory undertaker".
            NOTHING

-- paragraph 13.
-- src:2001 | 13. In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973, omit the definition
-- src:2002 | of “business” in section 61(1).
@ref sch para 13 (src:2001-2002)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch para 13 the definition of business in section 61(1) applies to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973, omit the definition of “business” in section 61(1)."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 13 speaks only of "a contract made before 18 May 1973"; a later contract is answered by s 61(1) and paragraph 12.
            NOTHING

