    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 1894))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Act applies to contracts of sale of goods made on or after (but not to those made before) 1 January 1894." -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 19 5 1985))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 19 May 1985, substitute the following for section 14" and "In relation to a contract made before 18 May 1973, substitute the following for section 14" -- the substituted section speaks of merchantable quality or of fitness, not of satisfactory quality (see the gates above and fork F8). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 14(2) there is an implied condition that the goods supplied are of satisfactory quality` `the seller sells the goods in the course of a business`

-- Gap found on review (2026-11-05): s 61(1) "business" took no date; paragraph 12 changes the definition for 18 May 1973 to 31 January 1978 and paragraph 13 omits it for an earlier contract.
-- src:189 | 1.—(1) This Act applies to contracts of sale of goods made on or
